    "content": {
      "question_html": "<p>A potential divider consists of a 6.0 V supply connected across a 10 kΩ fixed resistor in series with a thermistor. At 20 °C the thermistor has a resistance of 15 kΩ.</p>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Calculate the potential difference across the thermistor at 20 °C.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(2)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Explain what happens to this potential difference as the temperature rises.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(2)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">V = 6.0 × <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"frac__n\">15</span><span class=\"frac__d\">10 + 15</span></span></div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">V = 3.6 V</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">The resistance of the thermistor decreases</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">It takes a smaller share of the supply p.d., so the p.d. across it decreases</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
  },
