      "question_html": "<p>A 2.0 kW kettle heats 1.5 kg of water from 20 °C to 100 °C. The specific heat capacity of water is 4200 J kg<sup>−1</sup> K<sup>−1</sup>.</p>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Calculate the energy needed.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(2)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Calculate the minimum time taken.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(c)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Suggest why the actual time is longer.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(1)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Use of ΔE = mcΔθ = 1.5 × 4200 × 80</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">= 5.0 × 10<sup>5</sup> J</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">t = <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"frac__n\">5.04 × 10<sup>5</sup></span><span class=\"frac__d\">2000</span></span> = 250 s</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(c)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Energy is transferred to the surroundings and to the kettle itself</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
  },
